  "theorems": [
    "Positive singleton mass forces T_1 beta-scale and every fixed T_s/T_1 to have sub-beta logarithmic size.",
    "A bounded-degree primitive polynomial is beta-scale when its leading homogeneous form is at least T_1^d divided by a sub-beta factor.",
    "For the reciprocal transform Phi=H(e_1,...,e_k), one-sign monomial coefficients imply |H(T)|/T_1^d>=A^(-2kd)N^(-d).",
